        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fa7f4a93-b7b7-58b6-9291-05c30308a3c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Energy Northwest, Washington Public Power Supply System (WPPSS)\n- Projects: WNP-3, WNP-5, Satsop Nuclear Power Plant\n- Places: Pacific Northwest\n- Topics: nuclear power plant construction, projected electricity demand\n\nFacts:\n- Energy Northwest, formerly the Washington Public Power Supply System, was formed by Washington state law in 1957 as a United States public power joint operating agency.\n- Energy Northwest was created to produce at-cost power for Northwest utilities.\n- Washington Nuclear Project Nos. 3 and 5, abbreviated WNP-3 and WNP-5, were collectively known as the Satsop Nuclear Power Plant.\n- WNP-3 and WNP-5 were two of the five nuclear power plants whose construction was started by the Washington Public Power Supply System.\n- The Washington Public Power Supply System started construction on WNP-3 and WNP-5 to meet projected electricity demand in the Pacific Northwest.",
